---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' });
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Use | txttocsv"
  description="The terms that govern your use of txttocsv, a free browser-based TXT and CSV converter. Covers acceptable use, no-warranty on conversions, and limitation of liability."
>
  <article class="wrap section article">
    <nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <span>Terms</span></nav>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated on {updated}</p>

    <h2>Acceptance</h2>
    <p>By using txttocsv.com you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      txttocsv provides free, browser-based tools for converting between text and CSV files, along with
      related guides. The tools run on your device and are offered as-is.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the tools for lawful purposes only. You may not attempt to disrupt the site, scrape it at
      scale, or misrepresent it as your own service.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The converters are provided without warranty of any kind. While we test them carefully, you are
      responsible for verifying that any converted file is correct before you rely on it. Always keep a copy
      of your original data.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, txttocsv is not liable for any loss or damage arising from the
      use of, or inability to use, the site or its tools, including data loss.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms. The date above reflects the latest revision.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href="mailto:info@txttocsv.com">info@txttocsv.com</a>.</p>

    <p class="muted"><em>This is a general template. Adapt it to your jurisdiction and business entity before launch.</em></p>
  </article>
</Base>
